{"name":"Golden Delicious","hex":"#d2d88f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Golden Delicious","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A variety of apple which is pale yellow/green in color, and has a mild sweet flavour"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Golden_Delicious"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Delicious","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Delicious is a cultivar of apple from the United States, where it is one of the top varieties. Despite its name, it is not closely related to Red Delicious."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Golden_Delicious_apples.jpg/330px-Golden_Delicious_apples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Delicious","wikidata":"Q201996"},{"title":"Golden Delicious (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Delicious is a Canadian coming-of-age drama film, directed by Jason Karman and released in 2022. The film stars Cardi Wong as Jake, a Chinese Canadian teenager who must confront the expectations of his family when he joins the school basketball team in a bid to get closer to his classmate Aleks, with whom he has fallen in love."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Delicious_(film)","wikidata":"Q114964699"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Starr_070730-7802_Malus_pumila.jpg/500px-Starr_070730-7802_Malus_pumila.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Starr_070730-7802_Malus_pumila.jpg